---
// Template drafted for Wi-Fi Pros; have a lawyer review before relying on it.
import Layout from "../components/layouts/Layout.astro";
import Section from "../components/Section.astro";
import { business } from "../data/business";

const lastUpdated = "August 1, 2026";
---

<Layout
  title="Terms & Conditions | Wi-Fi Pros"
  description="The terms and conditions governing your use of the Wi-Fi Pros Network Consulting website."
>
  <Section border={false} class="pt-20">
    <h1>Terms &amp; Conditions</h1>
    <p class="mt-5 text-slate max-w-xl text-lg">
      Last updated: {lastUpdated}
    </p>
  </Section>

  <Section>
    <div class="article-body max-w-2xl">
      <p>
        These terms govern your use of the wifipros.ca website, operated by
        {business.legalName} ("we," "us," or "our"). By using this site, you agree
        to these terms. If you don't agree, please don't use the site.
      </p>

      <h2>Use of This Website</h2>
      <p>
        You may browse this website and use the contact and quote request forms
        for their intended purpose — learning about our services and reaching
        out to us. You agree not to misuse the site, including by submitting
        false information, attempting to disrupt the site's operation, or using
        automated tools to scrape or spam our forms.
      </p>

      <h2>Website Information, Not a Binding Offer</h2>
      <p>
        The content on this website — including service descriptions, example
        pricing language like "free quote," and general information about
        equipment or installation methods — is provided for general information
        only. It does not constitute a binding quote, offer, or contract. A
        quote request submitted through this site is the start of a
        conversation, not a confirmed order; actual pricing, scope, and
        scheduling are confirmed separately once we've discussed your property
        and requirements.
      </p>

      <h2>Third-Party Hardware</h2>
      <p>
        Where we install third-party hardware (such as Ubiquiti UniFi or UISP
        equipment), that hardware is covered by its manufacturer's warranty, not
        by this website. Any workmanship or service warranty we offer is set out
        separately in the agreement covering your specific project, not by these
        terms.
      </p>

      <h2>No Warranty on Website Content</h2>
      <p>
        We try to keep this website accurate and up to date, but we make no
        guarantees about its completeness or accuracy. The site and its content
        are provided "as is," without warranties of any kind.
      </p>

      <h2>Limitation of Liability</h2>
      <p>
        To the extent permitted by law, {business.legalName} is not liable for any
        indirect, incidental, or consequential damages arising from your use of this
        website. Nothing in this section limits liability that can't be limited under
        applicable law, or affects the terms of any separate service agreement between
        you and us.
      </p>

      <h2>External Links</h2>
      <p>
        This site may link to third-party websites (such as manufacturer pages).
        We aren't responsible for the content, accuracy, or privacy practices of
        sites we don't operate.
      </p>

      <h2>Intellectual Property</h2>
      <p>
        The content, design, and branding of this website belong to{" "}
        {business.legalName} unless otherwise noted, and may not be copied or reused
        without our permission.
      </p>

      <h2>Governing Law</h2>
      <p>
        These terms are governed by the laws of the Province of Alberta and the
        federal laws of Canada applicable in Alberta.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes to These Terms</h2>
      <p>
        We may update these terms from time to time. Changes will be posted on
        this page with an updated "Last updated" date.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact Us</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about these terms? Contact us at{" "}
        <a href={`mailto:${business.email}`}>{business.email}</a> or{" "}
        <a href={`tel:${business.phone.replace(/[^\d+]/g, "")}`}>
          {business.phone}
        </a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Section>
</Layout>
